course: dictionary
lesson: 2165
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Context, meaning the words around a word, tells you which meaning the writer means. «The Sun's thin outer atmosphere, the corona, is over a million degrees.» Here corona is a part of the Sun, not a virus or a crown.
explain: Corona is also a short word for coronavirus, the illness behind the COVID-19 pandemic. When people talked about lockdowns and home learning, corona meant that illness. Always ask: which meaning fits here? Try it in the sentence and see if it makes sense.
explain: The word comes from Latin for «crown», which fits a glowing ring of light around something. If the clues are still unclear, check a dictionary.
fact: Corona has three meanings: the hot outer layer of the Sun, a short name for coronavirus, and a ring of light around something.
fact: The Sun's corona can be seen as a glowing ring only during a total solar eclipse.
fact: The corona is over a million degrees, much hotter than the Sun's visible surface, the photosphere, at about 5,500 degrees Celsius.
fact: In recent history, «corona» was everyday talk for the COVID-19 pandemic, with lockdowns and home learning.
exercise: «The Sun's thin outer atmosphere, the corona, is over a million degrees.» What is the corona in this sentence? | A small planet | A virus that makes people ill | *The hot outer layer of gas around the Sun | A ring of light on a cake
exercise: During lockdown, a friend says, «Corona has closed our school.» What does corona mean here? | A glowing ring around the Moon | *Short for coronavirus, the illness behind the pandemic | A crown worn by a king | The hot outer layer of the Sun
exercise: The word corona comes from Latin. What does the Latin word mean? | A cloud | A star | A bridge | *A crown
test: During a total solar eclipse, astronomers can see the Sun's corona as what? | A loud bang | *A glowing ring | A cold blue lake | A shadow on the ground
test: Which sentence uses corona to mean a ring of light? | Corona closed our school for two months. | The corona was discussed on the news every night. | The class learned about the Sun at home. | *A bright corona of light circled the street lamp in the fog.
exam: Which is hotter, according to the text: «The Sun's visible surface, the photosphere, is about 5,500 degrees Celsius, but its thin outer atmosphere, the corona, is over a million degrees»? | They are the same temperature | *The corona | The photosphere | It depends on the eclipse
